Thank you Prof. Dean for the answer. Just a follow-up Q. Is there a lower limited on the number of landmarks that should be included in PLS?

A sample code to illustrate my question here:

require(Morpho) #for gorf.dat data (8 landmarks, 2D, 30 specimens)

library(shapes)

library(geomorph)

proc <- procSym(gorf.dat)

dim(proc$rotated)

plsa <- two.b.pls(proc$rotated[1:4,,],proc$rotated[5:8,,]) # 4 landmarks per module

plsb <- two.b.pls(proc$rotated[1,,],proc$rotated[5,,]) # 1 landmark per module

dim(plsa$XScores) gives a matrix of 30*8, while dim(plsb$XScores) gives a matrix of 2*30. No error is thrown for plsb, but the numbers in plsb$XScores are very strange:

