This may be a path forward. TPS grids are a function-based representation of shape deformation on the whole, not just landmark by landmark.

Of course, one should take some caution in interpreting differences across deformations; particularly for those areas where there are no landmarks. TPS grids form a suggestive view of shape change, but all of the shape information is grounded in the landmarks, not the spaces in-between (see early work from GMM and from engineering to recall this point).

