Hi folks,
I am trying to assess allometry in my dataset using procD.lm ( )  and using Sex, Sites and Species as factors.
My problem I think is about data manipulations with arrays and lists within geomorph.
I have several NAs in the variable Sex and can not include this model because I have 3 factors (female, males and NA) instead of two (female, male).

I will really appreciate it if someone can help me with the code to subset my dataset, filtering specimens and data associated with these NA.

Below my code

# import datasets
dorsal <- readland.tps("./data/dorsal.tps", specID = "imageID")
classifier_dor <- read.csv(file = "./data/dor_classifier.csv", header = TRUE, na.strings = c("NA",""))
# run gpa analysis
gpa_dorsal <- gpagen(dorsal, curves= NULL)
# create a geomorph.data.frame
gdf_dorsal <- geomorph.data.frame(gpa_dorsal, Sex= classifier_dor$sexo, Sites = classifier_dor$sites,
                                  Species= classifier_dor$species)

Thanks in advance

Julio

