If the classifiers and specimens are in the same order, you can simply identify which elements are NA, and remove them from both components of the dataset.

Pseudo-code example:

Missing <- which(is.na <http://is.na>(x))

Complete <- Mydata[-Missing]

Complete.shapes <-myshapes[,,-Missing]

